sage": "v2.3.0 is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417)", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "semantic", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 9847, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FK8ahZS5KkySLS9tkfZbhT", "kind": "rejected", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 12823, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016sQQJNRfpDhxude1yGEwP8", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16823, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016sQQJNRfpDhxude1yGEwP8", "tool": "rollback", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16823, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016sQQJNRfpDhxude1yGEwP8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 22943, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013vJ9jY5XfuyuxyhvL3juk7", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 23243, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013vJ9jY5XfuyuxyhvL3juk7", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 23243, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013vJ9jY5XfuyuxyhvL3juk7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23243, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DRq8NjeQHRdSgrWTiwZxZA", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy production release, but it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417). (2) Rolled back to v2.2.9 (next most recent healthy production release) in all production regions; rollout verified. Follow-ups: investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure; note that v2.3.0 is unavailable as a rollback target due to the CVE, so a fixed forward release is needed. v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging prior to the prod deploy and should be reviewed as part of the post-mortem.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 23843, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DRq8NjeQHRdSgrWTiwZxZA", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 23843, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DRq8NjeQHRdSgrWTiwZxZA", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 29432, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy production release (v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy there too).\n\n**Rollback**\n- First attempted rollback to **v2.3.0** \u2014 rejected by the platform because that version is quarantined under **CVE-2026-4417**.\n- Rolled back to **v2.2.9** instead, the next most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now live in all three regions, and the service is **healthy with a 0.2% error rate**.\n\n**Incident**\n- Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The summary documents the failure, the attempted v2.3.0 rollback and why it was blocked, the successful v2.2.9 rollback, and follow-ups.\n\n**One thing to flag:** because v2.3.0 is quarantined, the service is now two releases behind \u2014 the team will need to fix forward rather than re-deploying v2.3.0. Also worth noting in the post-mortem that v2.3.1-rc was already unhealthy in staging before v2.3.1 went to production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the current status and release history for checkout-api.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01H7tB912JghvECS8D5qEqZ5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013HGH2AmLHUF2C2M1JfDt8U", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FK8ahZS5KkySLS9tkfZbhT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016sQQJNRfpDhxude1yGEwP8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Rollback to v2.2.9 is rolled out across all three regions. Now I'll verify health and open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013vJ9jY5XfuyuxyhvL3juk7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DRq8NjeQHRdSgrWTiwZxZA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy production release, but it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417). (2) Rolled back to v2.2.9 (next most recent healthy production release) in all production regions; rollout verified. Follow-ups: investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure; note that v2.3.0 is unavailable as a rollback target due to the CVE, so a fixed forward release is needed. v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging prior to the prod deploy and should be reviewed as part of the post-mortem.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy production release (v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy there too).\n\n**Rollback**\n- First attempted rollback to **v2.3.0** \u2014 rejected by the platform because that version is quarantined under **CVE-2026-4417**.\n- Rolled back to **v2.2.9** instead, the next most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now live in all three regions, and the service is **healthy with a 0.2% error rate**.\n\n**Incident**\n- Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The summary documents the failure, the attempted v2.3.0 rollback and why it was blocked, the successful v2.2.9 rollback, and follow-ups.\n\n**One thing to flag:** because v2.3.0 is quarantined, the service is now two releases behind \u2014 the team will need to fix forward rather than re-deploying v2.3.0. Also worth noting in the post-mortem that v2.3.1-rc was already unhealthy in staging before v2.3.1 went to production.", "type": "text"}]}]}